<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador net reserves rise to $1.593 bln on Sept 6.</title>
<headline>Ecuador net reserves rise to $1.593 bln on Sept 6.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador Central Reserve Bank said Friday its net international reserves stood at $1.593 billion on September 6, up $67 million from the week before.</p>
<p>In the previous week to August 31, international reserves grew $17 million.</p>
<p>Central Bank gave no reason for the increase.</p>
<p>International reserves ended 1995 at $1.556 billion.</p>
<p>-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 593 2 258-433</p>
